    sections: [
      { h2: "What is footwear fulfillment?", body: "Footwear fulfillment is the receiving, storage, pick, pack, and shipping of shoe orders on a brand's behalf, handled so that size and variant accuracy, box condition, and returns are managed correctly. It differs from standard ecommerce fulfillment because footwear carries deep size runs per style, the retail shoebox must reach the customer undamaged, and return rates are high enough to need a dedicated inspection and restocking step. Delivery Group Inc. runs footwear fulfillment as a shoe 3PL, covering receiving through outbound shipping plus FBA prep, kitting, and returns from its Northern Kentucky operation." },
      { h2: "How does Delivery Group Inc. handle shoe size and variant accuracy?", body: "We track every footwear SKU down to the size and variant so the exact pair a customer ordered is the pair that ships. Shoe catalogs multiply fast: one style in ten sizes across three colors is thirty SKUs before any width or bundle options. Our pick system logs each unit by SKU, location, and lot, so a size 10 in one colorway never gets confused with a size 11 in another. Size, color, and width are tracked as distinct SKUs, picks are scan-verified to stop wrong-size ships, and deep size-run inventory is kept in sync across channels. That matters more in footwear than in almost any category, because a wrong size is an automatic return and a lost customer." },
      { h2: "How do you protect the shoebox during packing?", body: "We pack every pair so the retail shoebox reaches the customer in sellable condition, because for footwear the box is part of the product. A crushed or scuffed shoebox reads as a damaged order even when the shoes are perfect, and it drives returns and negative reviews. Our packers add protective outer packaging sized to the shoebox, use right-sized cartons to prevent shifting and crushing, and flag fragile and premium styles for extra care, so the box is not thrown loose into an oversized carton. For brands that want an unboxing moment, we support branded inserts and retail-ready presentation." },
      { h2: "How do you handle high footwear return rates?", body: "We run full returns processing for footwear, with inspection and restocking, because shoes come back more often than most categories. Sizing is hard to get right online, so returns are a normal part of a shoe business, not a failure. Every returned pair is inspected: sellable pairs are repackaged and restocked, including a shoebox check, so you are not writing off good inventory, and damaged or worn pairs are flagged rather than resold. We relabel and repack where needed and identify units that cannot go back to stock. Getting good pairs back to sellable fast is where a shoe 3PL either protects your margin or bleeds it." },
      { h2: "Why choose Delivery Group Inc. as your footwear 3PL?", body: "The difference is accuracy on the way out, care in the box, and a real plan for returns coming back. Our Northern Kentucky location sits next to the Cincinnati and CVG hub, so inbound freight and outbound shipments move quickly, and we receive most inventory the same day it arrives. We hit a consistent 48-hour turnaround on Amazon FBA prep, so new drops become sellable fast. Above all we treat footwear as its own category rather than a generic box to pick, which is what keeps wrong-size ships and crushed shoeboxes off your return report." },
    ],
    whyLabel: "Why Delivery Group",
    whyHeading: "Footwear treated as its own category, from variant accuracy to returns.",
    whyBullets: ["Every size, color, and width tracked as its own SKU, with scan-verified picks", "Careful, right-sized boxing so the retail shoebox arrives clean", "Inspection and restocking built in for high shoe return rates", "Same-day receiving in most cases and 48-hour FBA prep, near the Amazon CVG hub"],
